%description:

Tcp.ecnWillingness:conflict -- true with tcpEcnMode "accecn" stops the run with an error.

The claim: true replaces "off" or "passive" only.

The classes: off (false, the default: tcpEcnMode decides), on (true: "rfc3168" in place of
"off" or "passive"), conflict (true with a tcpEcnMode that requests ECN: an error). The code:
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables().

Host under test: host1, with tcpEcnMode "accecn". Observation: the error, and the exit code of
the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.ecnWillingness
%# class: conflict
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.ecnWillingness
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpEcnWillingnessConflict compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.ecnWillingness = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
Set the deprecated ecnWillingness or tcpEcnMode, not both
